// OpenWar3 override — `UI\FrameDef\Glue\LocalMultiplayerJoin.fdf`.
//
// One line the 2003 screen has no frame for, because the 2003 game never needed it: WHETHER
// OTHER MACHINES CAN REACH THIS ONE, and at what address.
//
// Real WC3 broadcast on the local subnet, so nobody typed an address and nobody could be
// unreachable in a way the screen had to explain. A browser can do neither — it cannot send a
// datagram, and it cannot find out whether anything outside this machine can reach it. What CAN
// know is the server that is serving this page, and it reports both with the handshake
// (`HostInfo`, src/net/protocol.ts); this is where that report is printed.
//
// It is a frame of its own rather than more text on `CustomCreateInfo` because that frame is
// ONE LINE — a TEXT is exactly its font tall (ui/fdf/layout.ts) and JUSTIFYMIDDLE grows a long
// string in BOTH directions, so a second line lands on top of "Local Area Network" above it.
// Measured: the info line's box is 0.245 wide, which is about 37 characters, and neither the
// address nor the diagnosis fits beside the sentence already there.
//
// It sits in the empty panel under that sentence and to the LEFT of the Create Game button,
// which is the space this screen has: the button's backdrop starts 0.213 in from the panel's
// left margin, so the width below is that gap less a small gutter. The Height is THREE lines
// of this font measured in the running screen rather than computed — a TEXT is clipped to its
// own box, and a line box is taller than the font size — and three is also all the panel has
// room for, so the strings that go here are written to that budget (src/net/lobby.ts
// `reachabilityLine`). JUSTIFYTOP, so it grows DOWNWARD from under the info line rather than
// back over it.

Frame "TEXT" "NetworkStatusText" INHERITS "StandardInfoTextTemplate" {
    Width 0.205,
    Height 0.052,
    FontJustificationH JUSTIFYLEFT,
    FontJustificationV JUSTIFYTOP,
    SetPoint TOPLEFT, "CustomCreateInfo", BOTTOMLEFT, 0.0, -0.004,
}

// Join a game on ANOTHER machine — the button that opens the list of servers to watch.
//
// The 2003 client had no such control because it never needed one: it broadcast on the subnet
// and the games appeared. We cannot broadcast from a page, and the packaged game has no address
// bar to navigate with, so two copies of OpenWar3 on one network would never see each other. The
// addresses are a thing the player MANAGES, so they live in a dialog of their own
// (src/overrides/ui/JoinAddressDialog.fdf) and this is the way in.
//
// It is `CreateButton`'s own pair, frame for frame — a small-button backdrop, mirrored, holding a
// 0.128 `StandardButtonTemplate` inset 0.012 / -0.0165 — because it belongs to the same family of
// acts: one makes a game, the other says where to look for them. It carries NO
// `ControlShortcutKey`; the screen's letters are spoken for (Create, Join, Cancel) and a caption
// with no gilded letter is better than a second frame answering one that is taken.
//
// It sits directly ABOVE Create Game, in the band under the games list — which is the only place
// on this screen a piece of button chrome fits at all. The panel below holds its title, its info
// line and Create Game already, with 0.006 between the info line and the button, and the strip
// that looks like a margin beside the list is the 3D background showing through. So the LIST
// gives up 0.055 of its height — about four rows of a list sized for Battle.net's hundreds — and
// the button takes the band that opens up. That resize is declared in src/overrides/index.ts
// rather than restated here, because `GameListContainer` is a frame the install declares INSIDE
// its parent, which a same-named declaration of ours never displaces (see `FdfOverride.resize`).

Frame "BACKDROP" "ServersListBackdrop" INHERITS "StandardMenuSmallButtonBaseBackdrop" {
    BackdropMirrored,
    // Anchored to CREATE GAME, because being directly above it is the whole placement — the two
    // read as one column of acts. The 0.078 lifts it clear of the panel between them, which
    // holds its own title, its info line and Create Game with 0.006 to spare: measured off the
    // running screen (Create's chrome starts 0.078 below where this one's has to end), not
    // guessed, and it lands exactly against the bottom of the games list above.
    SetPoint BOTTOMLEFT, "CreateBackdrop", TOPLEFT, 0.0, 0.078,

    Frame "GLUETEXTBUTTON" "ServersListButton" INHERITS WITHCHILDREN "StandardButtonTemplate" {
        Width 0.128,
        SetPoint TOPLEFT, "ServersListBackdrop", TOPLEFT, 0.012, -0.0165,

        ButtonText "ServersListButtonText",
        Frame "TEXT" "ServersListButtonText" INHERITS "StandardButtonTextTemplate" {
        }
    }
}
